  "notes": "West's spade lead is taken by East with the ♠A. East's heart shift appears helpful, but South must be careful when West covers South's heart with the ♥K.\n\nSouth appears to have 12 tricks, 2 spades, 3 hearts, 6 diamonds, and the ♣A. If South tries to take these 12 tricks, however, he will find himself taking only 8.\n\nAfter winning the ♥A, the blockage in diamonds prevents South from enjoying dummy's long suit. South will be held to 2 diamond tricks. When clubs break badly, 3NT will fail.\n\nThe solution is to allow West to hold the ♥K at trick 2! This play limits South to only 2 heart tricks, but preserves the ♥A as an entry to dummy's diamonds.\n\nWest continues hearts but South can win in hand, unblock the ♦A and ♦K, and cross to the ♥A. South is able to run the diamonds and take 11 tricks.",
